1
00:00:02,467 --> 00:00:03,885
KATARA: Water.

2
00:00:04,761 --> 00:00:06,137
Earth.

3
00:00:06,763 --> 00:00:08,097
Fire.

4
00:00:08,890 --> 00:00:10,141
Air.

5
00:00:11,184 --> 00:00:15,146
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:15,396 --> 00:00:18,608
Then, everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:19,651 --> 00:00:22,529
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

8
00:00:22,612 --> 00:00:23,821
could stop them.

9
00:00:23,905 --> 00:00:26,574
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

10
00:00:27,367 --> 00:00:29,827
100 years passed,
and my brother and I discovered

11
00:00:29,911 --> 00:00:32,705
the new Avatar,
an airbender named Aang.

12
00:00:32,956 --> 00:00:35,083
And although
his airbending skills are great,

13
00:00:35,166 --> 00:00:37,752
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

14
00:00:37,835 --> 00:00:38,920
AANG: Oof.

15
00:00:39,128 --> 00:00:42,090
KATARA: But I believe
Aang can save the world.

16
00:01:00,737 --> 00:01:01,905
( CHIRPS )

17
00:01:03,949 --> 00:01:05,283
( GASPS )

18
00:01:07,869 --> 00:01:11,748
Waterbending bomb! Yeah!

19
00:01:13,041 --> 00:01:15,126
( SPLASH )

20
00:01:15,210 --> 00:01:16,586
( ICE SHATTERS )

21
00:01:16,670 --> 00:01:17,754
( LAUGHING )

22
00:01:17,837 --> 00:01:20,924
Sure, 5,000-year-old maps
from the Spirit Library.

23
00:01:21,007 --> 00:01:23,009
Just splash some water on them.

24
00:01:23,593 --> 00:01:25,095
Sorry.

25
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:27,430
( BIRDS CHIRPING )

26
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:32,936
So did you figure out
what route we're gonna take?

27
00:01:33,019 --> 00:01:36,314
SOKKA: Okay, we just got out of
the desert, so we must be around here.

28
00:01:36,398 --> 00:01:38,608
And we need to go to
Ba Sing Se, which is here.

29
00:01:38,692 --> 00:01:41,695
It looks like the only passage
connecting the south to the north

30
00:01:41,778 --> 00:01:44,072
is this sliver of land
called the Serpent's Pass.

31
00:01:44,155 --> 00:01:47,200
- You're sure that's the best way to go?
- It's the only way.

32
00:01:47,284 --> 00:01:49,744
I mean, it's not like we
have Appa to fly us there.

33
00:01:49,828 --> 00:01:51,162
Shush up about Appa.

34
00:01:51,288 --> 00:01:53,707
Can't you at least
try to be sensitive?

35
00:01:55,083 --> 00:01:56,835
Katara, it's okay.

36
00:01:56,918 --> 00:01:59,212
I know I was upset about
losing Appa before,

37
00:01:59,296 --> 00:02:01,798
but I just want to focus on
getting to Ba Sing Se

38
00:02:01,881 --> 00:02:04,718
and telling the Earth King
about the solar eclipse.

39
00:02:05,343 --> 00:02:09,597
Oh, well, okay.
I'm glad you're doing better.

40
00:02:09,681 --> 00:02:12,475
Then to Ba Sing Se we go.
No more distractions.

41
00:02:12,559 --> 00:02:14,936
Hello there, fellow refugees!

42
00:02:19,649 --> 00:02:22,068
So are you guys headed
to Ba Sing Se too?

43
00:02:22,152 --> 00:02:23,278
Sure are.

44
00:02:23,361 --> 00:02:26,281
We're trying to get there before
my wife, Ying, has her baby.

45
00:02:26,364 --> 00:02:29,034
Great. We can travel through
the Serpent's Pass together.

46
00:02:29,576 --> 00:02:31,411
The Serpent's Pass?

47
00:02:31,494 --> 00:02:34,122
Only the truly desperate
take that deadly route.

48
00:02:34,205 --> 00:02:37,083
Deadly route? Great pick, Sokka!

49
00:02:37,167 --> 00:02:38,668
Well, we are desperate.

50
00:02:38,752 --> 00:02:40,920
You should come with us to Full Moon Bay.

51
00:02:41,004 --> 00:02:43,423
Ferries take refugees
across the lake.

52
00:02:43,506 --> 00:02:45,842
It's the fastest
way to Ba Sing Se.

53
00:02:45,925 --> 00:02:48,845
And it's hidden so the Fire Nation
can't find it.

54
00:02:49,220 --> 00:02:52,557
Hmm, peaceful ferry ride or deadly pass?

55
00:03:02,442 --> 00:03:04,319
I can't believe how many people's lives

56
00:03:04,402 --> 00:03:06,446
have been uprooted
by the Fire Nation.

57
00:03:06,529 --> 00:03:08,365
We're all looking for a better life...

58
00:03:08,448 --> 00:03:09,449
( BABY CRIES )

59
00:03:09,532 --> 00:03:11,618
...safe behind the walls
of Ba Sing Se.

60
00:03:22,003 --> 00:03:24,672
Who would've thought
after all these years

61
00:03:24,756 --> 00:03:26,716
I'd return to the scene

62
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:31,388
of my greatest military disgrace
as a tourist?

63
00:03:31,471 --> 00:03:32,639
Look around.

64
00:03:32,722 --> 00:03:34,933
We're not tourists. We're refugees.

65
00:03:36,851 --> 00:03:38,019
Ugh!

66
00:03:38,103 --> 00:03:40,605
I'm sick of eating rotten food,
sleeping in the dirt.

67
00:03:40,688 --> 00:03:42,524
I'm tired of living like this.

68
00:03:42,607 --> 00:03:43,650
JET: Aren't we all?

69
00:03:47,821 --> 00:03:50,365
My name's Jet, and these
are my Freedom Fighters,

70
00:03:50,448 --> 00:03:52,075
Smellerbee and Longshot.

71
00:03:52,158 --> 00:03:53,159
Hey.

72
00:03:54,160 --> 00:03:55,245
Hello.

73
00:03:55,328 --> 00:03:56,538
Here's the deal.

74
00:03:56,621 --> 00:03:58,540
I hear the captain's eating like a king

75
00:03:58,623 --> 00:04:01,126
while all us refugees have
to feed off his scraps.

76
00:04:01,209 --> 00:04:03,086
Doesn't seem fair, does it?

77
00:04:03,169 --> 00:04:05,797
What sort of king
is he eating like?

78
00:04:05,880 --> 00:04:07,841
The fat, happy kind.

79
00:04:09,759 --> 00:04:12,178
You wanna help us
liberate some food?

80
00:04:17,892 --> 00:04:19,519
-( SPLASHES )
- I'm in.

81
00:04:27,068 --> 00:04:30,029
I told you already,
no vegetables on the ferry!

82
00:04:30,363 --> 00:04:31,656
One cabbage slug

83
00:04:31,739 --> 00:04:34,534
could destroy the entire
ecosystem of Ba Sing Se!

84
00:04:34,617 --> 00:04:36,494
- Security!
- Aah!

85
00:04:36,619 --> 00:04:39,038
( GROWLS )

86
00:04:39,164 --> 00:04:42,542
Gah, my cabbages!

87
00:04:42,667 --> 00:04:45,462
( SOBS )

88
00:04:47,547 --> 00:04:48,840
Next!

89
00:04:50,341 --> 00:04:52,927
Um, four tickets for the
ferry to Ba Sing Se, please.

90
00:04:53,052 --> 00:04:54,262
Passports?

91
00:04:54,387 --> 00:04:57,765
Uh, no one told us we
had to have passports.

92
00:04:57,891 --> 00:05:00,602
Don't you know who this is?
He's the Avatar.

93
00:05:00,727 --> 00:05:02,937
Ah, I see 50 Avatars a day.

94
00:05:03,062 --> 00:05:05,565
And by the way,
not a very impressive costume.

95
00:05:09,110 --> 00:05:10,111
( SQUAWKS )

96
00:05:10,195 --> 00:05:14,449
Besides, no animals allowed.
Do I need to call security?

97
00:05:14,991 --> 00:05:16,826
( BURPS )

98
00:05:16,951 --> 00:05:18,286
( SQUEAKS AND TRILLS )

99
00:05:18,411 --> 00:05:20,246
That won't be necessary.

100
00:05:20,371 --> 00:05:22,707
- Next!
- I'll take care of this.

101
00:05:23,791 --> 00:05:26,836
My name is Toph Beifong
and I need four tickets.

102
00:05:27,212 --> 00:05:31,299
Ah, the golden seal of the flying boar.

103
00:05:31,424 --> 00:05:35,470
It is my pleasure to help
anyone of the Beifong family.

104
00:05:35,595 --> 00:05:37,138
It is your pleasure.

105
00:05:37,263 --> 00:05:38,640
As you can see,

106
00:05:38,765 --> 00:05:41,935
I am blind and these
three imbeciles are my valets.

107
00:05:42,060 --> 00:05:44,979
- But the animal―
- Is my seeing-eye lemur.

108
00:05:45,063 --> 00:05:46,064
( CHATTERS )

109
00:05:46,731 --> 00:05:49,400
Well, normally it's only one ticket
per passport,

110
00:05:49,526 --> 00:05:52,487
but this document
is so official,

111
00:05:52,612 --> 00:05:54,697
I guess it's worth four tickets.

112
00:05:57,408 --> 00:05:58,451
Thank you very much.

113
00:05:59,994 --> 00:06:01,871
All right!
We scammed that lady good!

114
00:06:01,996 --> 00:06:03,414
Aah!

115
00:06:03,540 --> 00:06:06,626
- Tickets and passports, please.
- Is there a problem?

116
00:06:06,751 --> 00:06:08,962
Yeah, I got a problem with you.

117
00:06:09,087 --> 00:06:10,755
I've seen your type before.

118
00:06:10,880 --> 00:06:13,132
Probably sarcastic,
think you're hilarious.

119
00:06:13,258 --> 00:06:16,052
And let me guess,
you're traveling with the Avatar.

120
00:06:16,636 --> 00:06:17,887
Do I know you?

121
00:06:18,513 --> 00:06:21,099
You mean you don't remember?
Maybe you remember this.

122
00:06:23,560 --> 00:06:24,561
Suki!

123
00:06:25,937 --> 00:06:27,647
Sokka, it's good to see you!

124
00:06:28,898 --> 00:06:33,152
KATARA: You look so different
without your makeup and the new outfit.

125
00:06:33,236 --> 00:06:35,947
That crabby lady makes all
the security guards wear them.

126
00:06:36,406 --> 00:06:39,200
And look at you, sleeveless guy.
Been working out?

127
00:06:39,284 --> 00:06:41,786
Oh, I'll grab a tree branch
and do a few chin touches

128
00:06:41,869 --> 00:06:43,997
every now and then. Nothing major.

129
00:06:45,707 --> 00:06:47,584
Are the other Kyoshi Warriors around?

130
00:06:47,667 --> 00:06:51,337
Yeah. After you left Kyoshi,
we wanted to find a way to help people.

131
00:06:51,421 --> 00:06:54,632
We ended up escorting some refugees,
and we've been here ever since.

132
00:06:54,757 --> 00:06:56,134
-( CHATTERS )
-( LAUGHS )

133
00:06:56,217 --> 00:06:58,094
Hi, Momo. Good to see you too.

134
00:06:58,177 --> 00:06:59,470
( TRILLS )

135
00:06:59,554 --> 00:07:01,931
So why are you guys getting
tickets for the ferry?

136
00:07:02,015 --> 00:07:03,808
Wouldn't you just fly across on Appa?

137
00:07:05,226 --> 00:07:06,603
Appa is missing.

138
00:07:06,728 --> 00:07:09,022
We hope to find him in Ba Sing Se.

139
00:07:09,147 --> 00:07:12,650
I'm so sorry to hear that.
Are you doing okay?

140
00:07:16,529 --> 00:07:17,697
I'm doing fine.

141
00:07:17,822 --> 00:07:19,782
Would everybody stop
worrying about me?

142
00:07:19,907 --> 00:07:22,744
Avatar Aang, you have to help us!

143
00:07:22,869 --> 00:07:24,746
Someone took all of our belongings,

144
00:07:24,871 --> 00:07:28,708
our passports, our tickets.
Everything's gone!

145
00:07:28,791 --> 00:07:29,792
( SOBS )

146
00:07:29,876 --> 00:07:31,544
I'll talk to the lady for you.

147
00:07:33,046 --> 00:07:35,006
No passports, no tickets!

148
00:07:36,466 --> 00:07:38,926
But she's pregnant, and
all their stuff was stolen.

149
00:07:39,010 --> 00:07:40,637
You have to make an exception.

150
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:41,888
No exceptions!

151
00:07:42,221 --> 00:07:44,682
If I just gave away tickets
willy-nilly to anyone,

152
00:07:44,766 --> 00:07:46,392
there would be no more order.

153
00:07:46,476 --> 00:07:49,270
And you know what that means―
no more civilization!

154
00:07:49,354 --> 00:07:50,897
What if we gave
them our tickets?

155
00:07:50,980 --> 00:07:51,981
- No!
- But―

156
00:07:52,065 --> 00:07:53,066
- Next!
-( SPITS )

157
00:07:54,317 --> 00:07:56,819
Don't worry, you'll
get to the city safely.

158
00:07:57,236 --> 00:07:59,197
I'll lead you through the Serpent's Pass.

159
00:08:06,871 --> 00:08:08,706
I can't believe we gave up our tickets

160
00:08:08,790 --> 00:08:11,000
and now we're going through
the Serpent's Pass.

161
00:08:11,084 --> 00:08:13,419
I can't believe you're
still complaining about it.

162
00:08:13,503 --> 00:08:14,504
I'm coming too!

163
00:08:15,880 --> 00:08:17,632
Are you sure that's a good idea?

164
00:08:17,715 --> 00:08:19,592
Sokka, I thought you'd want me to come.

165
00:08:19,717 --> 00:08:20,718
I do. It's just―

166
00:08:20,843 --> 00:08:22,470
Just what?

167
00:08:22,595 --> 00:08:24,180
Nothing. I'm glad you're coming.

168
00:08:29,310 --> 00:08:31,187
This is the Serpent's Pass?

169
00:08:31,270 --> 00:08:32,897
I thought it would be more wind-y.

170
00:08:32,980 --> 00:08:36,109
You know, like a serpent.
Hmm, I guess they misnamed it.

171
00:08:36,192 --> 00:08:39,028
Look at this writing. How awful.

172
00:08:39,112 --> 00:08:40,363
What does it say?

173
00:08:40,613 --> 00:08:42,782
It says, "Abandon hope."

174
00:08:43,408 --> 00:08:46,994
How could we abandon hope?
That's all we have.

175
00:08:47,120 --> 00:08:48,621
AANG: I don't know.

176
00:08:48,746 --> 00:08:51,582
The monks used to say that hope
is just a distraction.

177
00:08:51,708 --> 00:08:53,751
So maybe we do need to abandon it.

178
00:08:53,876 --> 00:08:55,253
What are you talking about?

179
00:08:56,129 --> 00:08:58,172
Hope isn't going to
get us into Ba Sing Se,

180
00:08:58,297 --> 00:09:00,007
and it's not gonna find Appa.

181
00:09:00,508 --> 00:09:02,760
We need to focus on what
we're doing right now,

182
00:09:02,844 --> 00:09:04,721
and that's getting across this pass.

183
00:09:06,681 --> 00:09:08,725
Okay, if you say so.

184
00:09:13,980 --> 00:09:16,232
SUKI: The Fire Nation
controls the Western Lake.

185
00:09:16,315 --> 00:09:19,277
Rumor has it they're working on
something big on the other side

186
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:21,696
and they don't want anyone
to find out what it is.

187
00:09:27,285 --> 00:09:28,286
Whoa!

188
00:09:28,369 --> 00:09:29,412
( GROANS )

189
00:09:31,539 --> 00:09:32,540
I'm okay!

190
00:09:33,124 --> 00:09:34,208
( RUMBLING )

191
00:09:34,292 --> 00:09:35,710
( SPLASH )

192
00:09:37,128 --> 00:09:38,129
They spotted us!

193
00:09:38,212 --> 00:09:39,380
Let's go! Let's go!

194
00:09:43,801 --> 00:09:45,344
( BLASTS )

195
00:09:48,681 --> 00:09:49,682
( GASPS )

196
00:09:56,397 --> 00:09:58,191
Suki, are you okay?

197
00:09:58,274 --> 00:10:00,526
You have to be more careful!
Come on!

198
00:10:01,694 --> 00:10:03,279
Thanks for saving my life, Toph.

199
00:10:03,362 --> 00:10:05,281
Hey, no problem, Sokka.

200
00:10:21,255 --> 00:10:23,466
Suki, you shouldn't
sleep there.

201
00:10:23,549 --> 00:10:25,176
Who knows how stable
this ledge is?

202
00:10:25,259 --> 00:10:26,803
It could give way at any moment.

203
00:10:26,886 --> 00:10:28,930
Sokka, I'm fine.
Stop worrying!

204
00:10:29,013 --> 00:10:30,640
You're right, you're right.

205
00:10:30,723 --> 00:10:33,184
You're perfectly capable
of taking care of yourself.

206
00:10:33,267 --> 00:10:34,393
Wait!

207
00:10:34,477 --> 00:10:37,230
Oh, never mind.
I thought I saw a spider. But you're fine.

208
00:11:10,805 --> 00:11:12,098
SMELLERBEE: Guard's coming!

209
00:11:32,702 --> 00:11:35,079
You know, it's okay to miss Appa.

210
00:11:36,831 --> 00:11:38,291
What's going on with you?

211
00:11:38,374 --> 00:11:40,835
In the desert, all you cared
about was finding Appa.

212
00:11:40,918 --> 00:11:43,254
And now it's like you don't
care about him at all.

213
00:11:43,337 --> 00:11:45,172
You saw what I did out there.

214
00:11:45,298 --> 00:11:48,759
I was so angry about losing
Appa, I couldn't control myself.

215
00:11:48,885 --> 00:11:50,636
I hated feeling like that.

216
00:11:50,761 --> 00:11:53,556
But now you're not letting
yourself feel anything.

217
00:11:53,681 --> 00:11:56,058
I know sometimes
it hurts more to hope,

218
00:11:56,183 --> 00:11:58,561
and it hurts more to care.

219
00:11:58,686 --> 00:12:01,230
But you have to promise me
that you won't stop caring.

220
00:12:02,815 --> 00:12:04,317
Come on, you need a hug.

221
00:12:05,818 --> 00:12:07,737
AANG: Thank you for you concern, Katara.

222
00:12:21,584 --> 00:12:24,170
- It's a beautiful moon.
- Yeah, it really is.

223
00:12:26,797 --> 00:12:28,716
Look, I know you're just trying to help,

224
00:12:28,841 --> 00:12:30,676
but I can take care of myself.

225
00:12:30,801 --> 00:12:32,053
I know you can.

226
00:12:32,178 --> 00:12:34,472
Then why are you
acting so overprotective?

227
00:12:34,555 --> 00:12:37,016
It's so hard to lose
someone you care about.

228
00:12:37,099 --> 00:12:38,893
Something happened at the North Pole

229
00:12:38,976 --> 00:12:40,686
and I couldn't protect someone.

230
00:12:40,770 --> 00:12:43,272
I don't want anything like
that to ever happen again.

231
00:12:43,356 --> 00:12:45,316
I lost someone I cared about.

232
00:12:45,441 --> 00:12:48,235
He didn't die. He just went away.

233
00:12:48,361 --> 00:12:50,488
I only had a few days
to get to know him,

234
00:12:50,613 --> 00:12:54,367
but he was smart,
and brave, and funny.

235
00:12:54,492 --> 00:12:57,662
Who is this guy?
Is he taller than me?

236
00:12:57,787 --> 00:12:59,664
No, he's about your height.

237
00:12:59,789 --> 00:13:02,792
- Is he better-looking?
- It is you, stupid!

238
00:13:02,917 --> 00:13:04,251
Oh.

239
00:13:11,968 --> 00:13:13,219
I can't.

240
00:13:13,844 --> 00:13:15,096
I'm sorry.

241
00:13:16,681 --> 00:13:18,766
No, you shouldn't be.

242
00:13:27,233 --> 00:13:29,694
So, Smellerbee.

243
00:13:29,777 --> 00:13:32,738
That's an unusual name for a young man.

244
00:13:32,905 --> 00:13:34,782
Maybe it's because I'm not a man.

245
00:13:34,907 --> 00:13:36,325
I'm a girl!

246
00:13:37,576 --> 00:13:39,912
Oh, now I see!

247
00:13:40,037 --> 00:13:43,207
It's a beautiful name for a lovely girl!

248
00:13:46,252 --> 00:13:48,170
I know. You're right.

249
00:13:48,295 --> 00:13:50,214
As long as I'm confident with who I am,

250
00:13:50,339 --> 00:13:52,550
it doesn't matter what
other people think.

251
00:13:52,675 --> 00:13:53,843
Thanks, Longshot.

252
00:13:56,429 --> 00:13:57,430
( SLURPING )

253
00:13:57,513 --> 00:13:58,931
From what I heard,

254
00:13:59,015 --> 00:14:01,851
people eat like this
every night in Ba Sing Se.

255
00:14:01,934 --> 00:14:04,395
I can't wait to set my
eyes on that giant wall.

256
00:14:04,562 --> 00:14:07,148
It is a magnificent sight.

257
00:14:07,273 --> 00:14:09,150
So you've been there before?

258
00:14:09,275 --> 00:14:13,529
Once, when I was a different man.

259
00:14:13,654 --> 00:14:16,574
I've done some things in my past
that I'm not proud of.

260
00:14:16,699 --> 00:14:19,118
But that's why I'm going to Ba Sing Se,

261
00:14:19,243 --> 00:14:22,371
for a new beginning,
a second chance.

262
00:14:22,496 --> 00:14:25,041
That's very noble of you.

263
00:14:25,166 --> 00:14:28,711
I believe people can change
their lives if they want to.

264
00:14:28,836 --> 00:14:30,713
I believe in second chances.

265
00:14:44,143 --> 00:14:45,394
( MOMO TRILLS )

266
00:14:53,110 --> 00:14:54,278
Everyone single file!

267
00:14:55,905 --> 00:14:57,073
( WATER RUSHING )

268
00:15:03,704 --> 00:15:05,414
KATARA: Aang, I need help!

269
00:15:05,790 --> 00:15:06,791
( CHATTERS )

270
00:15:28,646 --> 00:15:29,647
( FRIGHTENED CHATTER )

271
00:15:33,192 --> 00:15:34,235
What is that thing?

272
00:15:35,486 --> 00:15:36,487
( GASPING )

273
00:15:37,863 --> 00:15:40,366
( SCREAMING )

274
00:15:45,121 --> 00:15:47,081
( SPLASH )

275
00:16:02,721 --> 00:16:06,142
( ROARS )

276
00:16:06,225 --> 00:16:09,353
I think I just figured out why
they call it the Serpent's Pass!

277
00:16:10,187 --> 00:16:11,313
( ROARS )

278
00:16:14,775 --> 00:16:16,235
( ROARS )

279
00:16:17,319 --> 00:16:19,196
Suki, you know about
giant sea monsters.

280
00:16:19,280 --> 00:16:20,656
Make it go away!

281
00:16:20,739 --> 00:16:24,160
Just because I live near the Unagi
doesn't mean I'm an expert!

282
00:16:24,243 --> 00:16:26,620
Oh great and powerful sea serpent,

283
00:16:26,704 --> 00:16:28,914
please accept this humble
and tasty offering.

284
00:16:28,998 --> 00:16:30,666
- Thank you.
- Sokka!

285
00:16:31,083 --> 00:16:34,253
( SCREECHES )

286
00:16:34,336 --> 00:16:36,755
I'll distract it.
Katara, get everyone across.

287
00:16:36,839 --> 00:16:37,840
( ROARS )

288
00:16:43,053 --> 00:16:44,054
( SERPENT ROARS )

289
00:16:45,139 --> 00:16:46,473
( ROARS )

290
00:16:46,557 --> 00:16:47,892
( SCREECHES )

291
00:16:52,021 --> 00:16:53,230
( SCREECHES )

292
00:17:03,949 --> 00:17:05,284
( ROARS )

293
00:17:06,535 --> 00:17:07,536
( SCREECHES )

294
00:17:09,163 --> 00:17:10,623
Toph, come on! It's just ice!

295
00:17:13,250 --> 00:17:17,213
Actually, I'm gonna stay on my
little island where I can see.

296
00:17:17,296 --> 00:17:18,297
( SCREECHES )

297
00:17:18,380 --> 00:17:19,840
Aah! Okay, I'm coming!

298
00:17:22,343 --> 00:17:23,761
SOKKA: You're doing great!

299
00:17:23,886 --> 00:17:27,097
Just follow the sound of my voice.

300
00:17:27,181 --> 00:17:28,724
It's hard to ignore.

301
00:17:29,433 --> 00:17:31,352
SOKKA: You're almost there!

302
00:17:31,435 --> 00:17:33,604
-( SERPENT ROARS )
-( SCREAMS )

303
00:17:33,687 --> 00:17:36,023
Help! I can't swim!

304
00:17:37,024 --> 00:17:38,400
SOKKA: I'm coming, Toph!

305
00:17:40,110 --> 00:17:41,278
( SERPENT SCREECHES )

306
00:17:43,489 --> 00:17:45,574
-( PANTING )
- Help!

307
00:17:49,286 --> 00:17:50,704
( BUBBLING )

308
00:17:51,914 --> 00:17:53,207
( GASPS )

309
00:17:53,791 --> 00:17:56,835
Oh, Sokka, you saved me!

310
00:17:56,961 --> 00:17:58,796
Mwah!

311
00:17:58,879 --> 00:18:01,507
Actually, it's me.

312
00:18:01,590 --> 00:18:04,218
Oh, well. ( CHUCKLES )

313
00:18:04,301 --> 00:18:06,095
You can go ahead and
let me drown now.

314
00:18:07,596 --> 00:18:09,265
( ROARS )

315
00:18:17,231 --> 00:18:19,817
( SCREECHES )

316
00:18:22,736 --> 00:18:23,988
( SCREECHES )

317
00:18:30,786 --> 00:18:32,413
ALL: Yeah!

318
00:18:39,253 --> 00:18:40,254
There's the wall!

319
00:18:42,339 --> 00:18:45,467
Now it's nothing but smooth
sailing to Ba Sing Se.

320
00:18:45,551 --> 00:18:46,844
( GASPS ) Oh no!

321
00:18:46,927 --> 00:18:47,928
What's wrong?

322
00:18:48,637 --> 00:18:49,972
The baby's coming.

323
00:18:50,055 --> 00:18:51,598
What? Now?

324
00:18:51,682 --> 00:18:53,434
Can't you hold it in or something?

325
00:18:53,642 --> 00:18:54,810
Sokka, calm down.

326
00:18:54,893 --> 00:18:57,438
I helped Gran Gran deliver
lots of babies back home.

327
00:18:57,521 --> 00:19:00,441
This isn't the same as
delivering an arctic seal!

328
00:19:00,524 --> 00:19:03,861
This a real... Human... Thing!

329
00:19:04,320 --> 00:19:05,654
It's called a baby.

330
00:19:05,738 --> 00:19:07,990
And I've helped her deliver
plenty of those too.

331
00:19:08,073 --> 00:19:11,410
Aang, get some rags.
Sokka, water.

332
00:19:12,077 --> 00:19:15,497
Toph, I need you to make
an earth tent― A big one.

333
00:19:18,500 --> 00:19:19,752
Suki, come with me.

334
00:19:24,590 --> 00:19:26,967
You know, as soon
as I saw your scar,

335
00:19:27,051 --> 00:19:28,385
I knew exactly who you were.

336
00:19:29,970 --> 00:19:32,556
You're an outcast, like me.

337
00:19:32,639 --> 00:19:34,641
And us outcasts have
to stick together.

338
00:19:34,725 --> 00:19:39,188
We have to watch each other's
backs, because no one else will.

339
00:19:39,438 --> 00:19:43,400
I've realized lately that being on
your own isn't always the best path.

340
00:19:48,989 --> 00:19:51,700
( PANTING )

341
00:19:52,159 --> 00:19:55,079
You're doing great, Ying.
Sokka, where's that water?

342
00:19:55,329 --> 00:20:01,293
Now get ready to push.
One, two, three, push!

343
00:20:01,377 --> 00:20:03,379
( YING GROANS )

344
00:20:03,879 --> 00:20:05,839
( BABY CRYING )

345
00:20:05,923 --> 00:20:07,299
KATARA: It's a girl!

346
00:20:07,383 --> 00:20:09,385
So, you wanna go see the baby

347
00:20:09,468 --> 00:20:11,887
or are you going to faint
like an old lady again?

348
00:20:12,179 --> 00:20:13,847
No, no. I'm good this time.

349
00:20:20,437 --> 00:20:22,856
Aang, you have to come see this.

350
00:20:26,110 --> 00:20:27,319
( BABY CRYING )

351
00:20:27,486 --> 00:20:29,822
- She sounds healthy.
- She's beautiful.

352
00:20:30,781 --> 00:20:32,950
And so squishy-looking.

353
00:20:37,162 --> 00:20:38,580
What should we name her?

354
00:20:38,664 --> 00:20:41,583
I want our daughter's
name to be unique.

355
00:20:41,667 --> 00:20:43,585
I want it to mean something.

356
00:20:48,465 --> 00:20:51,260
I've been going through
a really hard time lately.

357
00:20:51,343 --> 00:20:53,679
But you've made
me hopeful again.

358
00:20:54,972 --> 00:20:57,057
I know what I want
to name our baby now.

359
00:20:57,766 --> 00:20:58,892
Hope.

360
00:20:59,393 --> 00:21:02,479
That's a perfect name. Hope.

361
00:21:06,233 --> 00:21:08,402
I thought I was
trying to be strong.

362
00:21:08,485 --> 00:21:11,363
But really I was just running
away from my feelings.

363
00:21:11,905 --> 00:21:15,993
Seeing this family together,
so full of happiness and love,

364
00:21:16,076 --> 00:21:18,454
it's reminding me
how I feel about Appa...

365
00:21:20,581 --> 00:21:22,416
...and how I feel about you.

366
00:21:30,299 --> 00:21:32,968
I promise, I'll find Appa
as fast as I can.

367
00:21:33,177 --> 00:21:34,803
I just really need to do this.

368
00:21:35,596 --> 00:21:37,055
See you in the big city.

369
00:21:37,139 --> 00:21:39,558
Say hi to that big fuzzball for me.

370
00:21:40,684 --> 00:21:43,061
- You'll find him, Aang.
- I know.

371
00:21:43,145 --> 00:21:44,354
Thank you, Katara.

372
00:21:46,356 --> 00:21:47,357
( CHATTERS )

373
00:21:47,441 --> 00:21:49,443
- You ready, Momo?
-( CHATTERS )

374
00:21:52,029 --> 00:21:53,989
( CHATTERS )

375
00:21:55,365 --> 00:21:57,576
Sokka, it's been really great
to see you again.

376
00:21:57,868 --> 00:21:59,328
Whoa, hold on.

377
00:21:59,411 --> 00:22:01,538
Why does it sound like
you're saying goodbye?

378
00:22:01,622 --> 00:22:03,665
I came along because
I wanted to make sure

379
00:22:03,749 --> 00:22:05,876
you got through
the Serpent's Pass safely.

380
00:22:05,959 --> 00:22:08,670
But now I need to get back
to the other Kyoshi Warriors.

381
00:22:08,921 --> 00:22:11,715
So you came along to protect me?

382
00:22:11,840 --> 00:22:15,886
Listen, I'm really sorry about last night.

383
00:22:16,303 --> 00:22:19,473
We were talking and saying things...

384
00:22:19,556 --> 00:22:21,850
I just got carried away
and before I knew it, I―

385
00:22:24,353 --> 00:22:25,729
You talk too much.

386
00:22:33,612 --> 00:22:35,239
( MOMO CHATTERS )

387
00:22:39,535 --> 00:22:40,536
( CHATTERS )

388
00:22:46,583 --> 00:22:47,834
( CHATTERS )

389
00:22:52,047 --> 00:22:53,298
( GASPS )

390
00:23:05,310 --> 00:23:08,021
Sorry, Momo. Appa's gonna have to wait.

391
00:23:08,355 --> 00:23:09,856
( DRILL WHIRRING )
